# devkitPro build output. Everything here is regenerated by `make` from source/, gfx/
# and the shader — none of it is authored, and the .elf alone is ~4 MB.
build/
build-host/
*.3dsx
*.smdh
*.elf
*.cia
*.bnr

# Host-side test output. Named build-<module> rather than build/ on purpose — a host .o left
# beside its source is found by the console build's VPATH scan, which then hands ld an object
# the ARM compiler never produced.
#
# A glob rather than a list, because the list fell behind: build-blockdiff/ and build-networld/
# were named here, but source/world/Makefile.inventory-persist-test writes build-inventory-persist/
# and never got an entry, so its 69 KB host binary sat untracked in `git status` long enough that
# nobody could remember what it was. Any Makefile or ad-hoc run that follows the build-<thing>/
# convention is now covered without a second edit. Does not match build/ — that is line 3.
build-*/

# Bytecode cache, written by the interpreter the moment one tools/ script imports another.
# tools/make_sounds.py importing tools/make_sfx_synth.py creates it, so it appears the first
# time anyone regenerates the audio and is pure build output.
__pycache__/

# Third-party and cross-repo sources fetched by `make deps`, both pinned to a commit:
# libhydrogen, and the gateway's bs_proto.h (the wire format, which is defined in the
# server repo and only mirrored here). Fetched, never authored — committing either would
# create a second editable copy that can drift from the thing it has to agree with.
deps/

# picasso and tex3ds intermediates, in case they are ever emitted in-tree.
*.shbin
*.shbin.h
*_shbin.h
*.t3x
*.t3s.d
